# Skill: Debug `bishengir-opt` (type A)

Use `scripts/debug_opt.sh` to run `bishengir-opt` with tracing on an `.mlir`
input and capture the full log. `bishengir-opt` is a standard MLIR opt driver
(`MlirOptMain`), so every `--mlir-print-ir-*`, `--debug`, `--debug-only=`,
`--verify-each` flag works, plus AscendNPU-IR passes and `--target=`.

## How to run

```bash
# Inspect IR before & after one pass
scripts/debug_opt.sh in.mlir -p "--your-pass" --around YourPass

# Full per-pass trace, split into one file per pass
scripts/debug_opt.sh in.mlir -p "-pass-pipeline=builtin.module(cse)" \
    --print-after-all --split-dumps ir_dumps/

# LLVM debug output scoped to a DEBUG_TYPE, A5 target
scripts/debug_opt.sh in.mlir --debug-only=hivm --target Ascend910_95 -- --mlir-timing
```

Key options: `-b/--bin`, `-p/--pass` (repeatable), `--target T`,
`--print-after-all`, `--print-before-all`, `--print-after PASS`,
`--print-before PASS`, `--around PASS`, `--print-after-change`,
`--print-after-failure`, `--debug`, `--debug-only X`, `--verify-each`,
`--split-dumps DIR`, `-o/--output FILE`, `-l/--log FILE`, `--dry-run`.

The binary auto-resolves from `--bin`, `$BISHENGIR_OPT`, `$ASCENDNPU_IR_BIN`,
`bishengir-output/bin`, `build/install/bin`, `build/bin`, then `PATH`.

## Agent guidance

- Threading is auto-disabled while printing IR so dumps stay ordered; pass
  `--keep-threading` only if you need parallelism.
- To debug a specific failing pass, use `--around <Pass>` (or `--print-before
  <Pass>`), read the before/after IR, and narrow from there.
- `--split-dumps` + the printed `index.txt` let you open the IR at each pass
  boundary individually — ideal input for bisecting which pass corrupts the IR.
- Report the real exit code and the log path; quote the relevant IR/diagnostic.
- Anything the wrapper doesn't expose goes after `--` verbatim.
